# capture.py regenerates every fixture and every intermediate from the vips
# binary and its own MAT-5 writer, so the whole tree here is reproducible
# with `python3 capture.py` and no Rust toolchain and no scipy.
#
# fixtures/ IS pinned: matload is load-only, so a port has no way to produce
# these inputs for itself and needs them checked in. They are 49 tiny files,
# under 10K in total, because MAT balloons fast and every array here is 2x2
# or 2x3.
#
# outputs/ holds the intermediate `.v` files every direct `vips matload`
# call writes, and is pure scratch.
outputs/
